tcp_mss_gso_test.py
===================

Description
-----------
Validates TCP MSS (Maximum Segment Size) handling and the kernel GSO
(Generic Segmentation Offload) disable behaviour for virtual network
devices (ibmvnic / virtio-net).

The test is designed to verify that the kernel patch which prevents
adapter freezes on small-MSS connections works correctly:

  * For MSS values **below** the GSO threshold (default 224 bytes), the
    kernel must emit a "MSS too small" warning and disable GSO.
  * For MSS values **at or above** the threshold the warning must NOT
    appear and GSO must remain active.

Test flow (per MSS value)
--------------------------
1. Deploy a bidirectional TCP echo listener on the remote (peer) host.
2. Add an iptables TCPMSS clamp rule on the SUT to force the desired MSS
   on outgoing SYN segments.
3. Run N socket-level large-send / echo iterations (default 64 KB payload).
4. Concurrently run:
     - HTTP background load (curl + wget against the peer web server)
     - iperf3 TCP stream (same MSS, via -M flag)
5. Check dmesg for the GSO-disable kernel warning.
6. Remove the iptables rule and repeat for the next MSS value.
7. After all MSS values: assert zero socket failures and correct
   GSO warning presence/absence.

Prerequisites
-------------
SUT (System Under Test)
  - Root / sudo access (required for iptables)
  - iptables, iperf3, curl, wget installed (test installs them if missing)
  - Python 3.6+

Remote (peer) host
  - SSH access with the credentials specified in the YAML
  - python3, iperf3 installed (test installs them if missing via SSH)
  - Optional: a web server (nginx/httpd) on port 80 for HTTP load
    (if enable_http_load is True)

Running the test
----------------
Populate tcp_mss_gso_test.yaml with your peer IP / credentials, then:

    avocado run io/net/virt-net/tcp_mss_gso_test.py \
        --mux-yaml io/net/virt-net/tcp_mss_gso_test.py.data/tcp_mss_gso_test.yaml

Quick single-MSS smoke test (override from command line):

    avocado run io/net/virt-net/tcp_mss_gso_test.py \
        --mux-yaml io/net/virt-net/tcp_mss_gso_test.py.data/tcp_mss_gso_test.yaml \
        -p peer_ip=192.168.1.10 -p mss_values=224,223 -p iterations=3

Parameters
----------
See tcp_mss_gso_test.yaml for full documentation of every parameter.

Key parameters:

  peer_ip           Remote host IP address  (REQUIRED)
  peer_user         SSH user                (default: root)
  peer_password     SSH password            (REQUIRED)
  mss_values        Comma-separated MSS list to sweep
                    (default: "1460,536,224,223,128,64,36,1")
  iterations        Socket-echo iterations per MSS  (default: 5)
  enable_http_load  Enable curl/wget background load (default: True)
  enable_iperf      Enable iperf3 background traffic (default: True)
  iperf_duration    iperf3 test duration in seconds  (default: 30)
  gso_threshold     MSS value boundary for GSO       (default: 224)
  data_size         Payload bytes per echo iteration (default: 65536)
  socket_timeout    Per-connection timeout in seconds (default: 30)

Output
------
The tearDown phase prints a summary table such as:

  MSS     GSO       Sock OK   Sock Fail   iperf Mbps  HTTP reqs  Avg KB/s
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1460    ON        5         0           9423.10     312        98432.0
   536    ON        5         0           9118.44     298        94120.3
   224    ON        5         0           4201.20     255        41280.1
   223    OFF       5         0           N/A         248        38910.6
   128    OFF       5         0           N/A         241        22440.2
    64    OFF       5         0           N/A         230        11200.5
    36    OFF       5         0           N/A         218         6300.1
     1    OFF       5         0           N/A         201          196.3

